        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Fix doctor completion cache plugin loading",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes the Windows `openclaw doctor` shell-completion cache path observed in the maintainer workshop: doctor was spawning `openclaw completion --write-state` without the plugin-command skip guard, so completion cache generation could load plugin CLI commands and trigger bundled runtime dependency work during doctor.\n\nThe update path already sets `OPENCLAW_COMPLETION_SKIP_PLUGIN_COMMANDS=1` for this same cache write. This applies the same guard to doctor-triggered completion cache writes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/commands/doctor-completion.test.ts src/cli/completion-cli.write-state.test.ts`\n- `pnpm exec oxlint src/commands/doctor-completion.ts src/commands/doctor-completion.test.ts`\n",
